                    {
                        "translation_id": "37179468-1dac-43ac-93d4-ee99496155ba",
                        "source_entry_id": "2797a93d-c11d-36d0-bb95-82d3781d7cd6",
                        "source_sense_id": "dff2c0bf-2aaa-390b-b981-cff436975bba",
                        "target_lang_word": "bemusement",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bemusement",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b39efee-b70a-3c86-8669-c20efa618ed2",
                                        "entry_id": "a4dc8f9e-d989-3a3b-9aa9-538c9efa47b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being bemused."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d8294f1-a352-4171-8404-102b42a4e04a",
                                                "sense_id": "2b39efee-b70a-3c86-8669-c20efa618ed2",
                                                "text": "Wrex touches his grandfather's armor, his expression… thoughtful, perhaps? Krogan are hard to read. Then he shakes off his bemusement and grips his gun with renewed purpose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2eae0ef-f79d-4104-8ec6-a75ea5d1cb05",
                                                "sense_id": "2b39efee-b70a-3c86-8669-c20efa618ed2",
                                                "text": "The response to this latest scandal has taken a familiar turn, dividing along gender lines. While senior women have condemned it, many of the Financial Times’ (male) readers have expressed unhappy bemusement at finding this article on the front page."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "115c7b37-b61e-4d89-8746-887ae30d466a",
                        "source_entry_id": "2797a93d-c11d-36d0-bb95-82d3781d7cd6",
                        "source_sense_id": "dff2c0bf-2aaa-390b-b981-cff436975bba",
                        "target_lang_word": "immersion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immersion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a2cd594-5910-3184-8a56-77446433444a",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of immersing or the condition of being immersed.",
                                            "The total submerging of a person in water as an act of baptism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d7274f1-6d63-4268-992b-26992f904819",
                                                "sense_id": "5a2cd594-5910-3184-8a56-77446433444a",
                                                "text": "Jesus did not become known as a baptizer (cf. however John 3:26 and 4:1), but we can recognize the same ritual structure in his healing practice as in John's immersion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "383014fb-e780-3b1f-a011-472ec2a3fbc7",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of immersing or the condition of being immersed.",
                                            "Deep engagement in something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ffad19c-e347-4147-bea2-59862c230f93",
                                                "sense_id": "383014fb-e780-3b1f-a011-472ec2a3fbc7",
                                                "text": "In examining Capote, Clarke follows the course of the precocious writer's life with painstaking attention to gossipy detail. It's an exhaustive roller coaster of a read, a high-tilt immersion into the social swirl and scandal that accompanied most of Capote's adult life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "416e0cb2-e81b-4c40-a6d1-b0640a8240d2",
                                                "sense_id": "383014fb-e780-3b1f-a011-472ec2a3fbc7",
                                                "text": "Recognising and knowing how to understand visual imagery in relation to a narrative in picture books is primarily a matter of immersion in books within a specific culture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18bb3421-94fe-3852-a73b-d2f3da3a993a",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An immersion heater."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "countable",
                                            "informal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5097fb51-613e-4901-a2fd-0f5fcb5bbadf",
                                                "sense_id": "18bb3421-94fe-3852-a73b-d2f3da3a993a",
                                                "text": "She left the immersion on all the time, while I had been reared under pain of death to turn it off as soon as the bathwater was heated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5448fbdc-56b9-3a63-8248-8c17a018fe8a",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A smooth map whose differential is everywhere injective, related to the mathematical concept of an embedding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab933d64-7c83-4a93-b622-08954c106c50",
                                                "sense_id": "5448fbdc-56b9-3a63-8248-8c17a018fe8a",
                                                "text": "Note that every embedding is an immersion, but the converse is not true. For an immersion to be an embedding, it must be one-to-one and the inverse must be continuous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "604c6597-885b-31de-9e03-ea43ed50342b",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The disappearance of a celestial body, by passing either behind another, as in the occultation of a star, or into its shadow, as in the eclipse of a satellite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa08d353-bd64-4497-825a-3c49f874c245",
                                                "sense_id": "604c6597-885b-31de-9e03-ea43ed50342b",
                                                "text": "An occultation of a star by the moon provides two sharply defined observable phenomena: the disappearance of a star behind the disc of the moon (called its immersion), and its subsequent reappearance (or emersion)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53cc5463-5d0a-37e9-bb51-59874ed6c606",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of foreign-language teaching where the language is used intensively to teach other subjects to a student."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5297253-4ff2-4ba0-afc3-ec013de43e5d",
                                                "sense_id": "53cc5463-5d0a-37e9-bb51-59874ed6c606",
                                                "text": "Although numerous studies have reported the effectiveness of immersion programmes in developing relatively high levels of second language proficiency without any tradeoff of first language development or subject matter mastery, little is known of immersion education in Japan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07bba890-7edd-3d99-acff-23bb19606450",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One's suspension of disbelief while reading, playing a video game, etc. The experience of losing oneself in a fictional world."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d5a4ab4-7448-3aaf-9369-ebdfbb1921c3",
                                        "entry_id": "6337562c-422a-313b-ad5a-a3b5a097c7d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A creative relationship with one's social and ecological environment as practiced by the Brooklyn Immersionists."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "601ac9fc-a7bf-41d4-8330-cd6bf57cb94b",
                        "source_entry_id": "2797a93d-c11d-36d0-bb95-82d3781d7cd6",
                        "source_sense_id": "dff2c0bf-2aaa-390b-b981-cff436975bba",
                        "target_lang_word": "preoccupation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "preoccupation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a88c8a6b-16eb-3522-b44d-3a1cc1297b4b",
                                        "entry_id": "84ca6e97-a755-3b61-830b-ef694af3d65a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being preoccupied or an idea that preoccupies the mind; enthrallment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b740fa7f-ba74-4e7b-9624-f48485781fd4",
                                                "sense_id": "a88c8a6b-16eb-3522-b44d-3a1cc1297b4b",
                                                "text": "Halalisation signifies a powerful and growing preoccupation with the proliferation of […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e3fc828-f6eb-41d1-80a4-691692dcb977",
                                                "sense_id": "a88c8a6b-16eb-3522-b44d-3a1cc1297b4b",
                                                "text": "At the same time that they invoke Christian identity, the civilizationists also stress their secularism. But there is no contradiction between the populist right’s Christianism and its secularism, since both derive from a preoccupation with Islam."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0324c1f-aba5-44c9-b9a3-d465b19a22d8",
                                                "sense_id": "a88c8a6b-16eb-3522-b44d-3a1cc1297b4b",
                                                "text": "The same preoccupation with developing a conceptual framework is evident in David Blank's Venezuela: Politics in a Petroleum Republic, a modified version of Blank's early theses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0658d51f-ed8f-470d-8001-9842f91909a7",
                                                "sense_id": "a88c8a6b-16eb-3522-b44d-3a1cc1297b4b",
                                                "text": "As an adult, I became a journalist whose beat is the environment. In a way, I’ve turned my youthful preoccupations into a profession."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "909e386b-fffe-4bbd-a669-b7c4530959a4",
                                                "sense_id": "a88c8a6b-16eb-3522-b44d-3a1cc1297b4b",
                                                "text": "Uncertain how to address a French preoccupation with security and immigration, and facing a generational fracture over identity politics, the left’s disarray has allowed Mr. Macron to tilt rightward for votes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8f7a949-0f2a-32b5-a322-6c7c3e5435a2",
                                        "entry_id": "84ca6e97-a755-3b61-830b-ef694af3d65a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of occupying something before someone else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3439b16c-330b-4a11-9444-477ede1e04f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "2797a93d-c11d-36d0-bb95-82d3781d7cd6",
                        "source_sense_id": "dff2c0bf-2aaa-390b-b981-cff436975bba",
